# You get up to go; Grandpa Park asks where you're going, too fast to catch. You ask him to say it again,
# and he says it slowly.
# Each <id>-alt<n> is a written wrong reply, using only words met by then; <id>-alt<n>-answer is the answer to it.

fast = 어디 가요?
fast-reply = 네?
fast-alt1 = 안녕하세요.
fast-alt2 = 감사합니다.

again = 어디 가요? 어디?
again-reply = 네? 다시요.
again-alt1 = 아니요.
again-alt2 = 네, 알아요.

slow = 어디…… 가요?
slow-reply = 몰라요.
slow-alt1 = 네, 알아요.
slow-alt2 = 안녕히 가세요.
